{
  "slug": "fullsail-2026-08",
  "kind": "protocol-exploit",
  "title": "Full Sail vaults drained through a Switchboard oracle key swap, 29 August 2026",
  "network": "mainnet",
  "summary": "On 29 August 2026 an attacker created three guardian oracles on Switchboard's guardian queue and used them to attest its own signing key onto a live Switchboard oracle; Switchboard v4's attestation check read the wrong oracle's expiry and accepted a guardian with an empty key. With that key it signed prices 100x below market into feeds Full Sail's vaults (ports) read, deposited, restored the price and withdrew, 63 times across three ports, for about $91,000. Switchboard shipped a fix at 06:37 UTC and Full Sail paused its ports from 05:29 UTC.",
