    {
      "id": "attest-checks-wrong-oracle",
      "question": "Which object does Switchboard v4's attestation check read to decide whether the guardian is valid?",
      "tool": "disassemble_module",
      "args": {
        "package_id": "{switchboard_v4}",
        "module_name": "oracle_attest_action",
        "function_name": "validate"
      },
      "expect": [
        {
          "path": "disassembly",
          "op": "matches",
          "value": "64: CopyLoc\\[0\\]\\(Arg0: &mut Oracle\\)\\s+65: FreezeRef\\s+66: Call oracle::expiration_time_ms\\(&Oracle\\): u64[\\s\\S]*Guardian is invalid"
        },
        {
          "path": "disassembly",
          "op": "matches",
          "value": "Call oracle::secp256k1_key\\(&Oracle\\): vector<u8>[\\s\\S]*Call hash::check_subvec"
        }
      ],
      "tier": "code-derived",
      "basis": "Chain (v4 bytecode, read with disassemble_module): the 'Guardian is invalid' check in validate reads expiration_time_ms of Arg0, the oracle being attested, not Arg2, the guardian; v5 changes instruction 64 to CopyLoc[2]. DeepSafe (citing MoveBit) describes a possible key-rotation authorisation bypass."
    },
    {
      "id": "empty-key-matches",
      "question": "Does v4's key comparison reject a guardian with no key?",
      "tool": "disassemble_module",
      "args": {
        "package_id": "{switchboard_v4}",
        "module_name": "hash",
        "function_name": "check_subvec"
      },
      "expect": [
        {
          "path": "disassembly",
          "op": "matches",
          "value": "^(?![\\s\\S]*is_empty)[\\s\\S]*CopyLoc\\[1\\]\\(Arg1: &vector<u8>\\)\\s+15: VecLen\\(16\\)\\s+16: StLoc\\[4\\][\\s\\S]*53: LdTrue\\s+54: Ret"
        }
      ],
      "tier": "code-derived",
      "basis": "Chain (v4 bytecode, read with disassemble_module): check_subvec loops over the length of its second argument and returns true when the loop ends, so an empty guardian key matches any recovered public key; v5 adds a vector::is_empty check that returns false."
    },
